{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>All who go forth to the army.</b> Scripture says this in all the details of the count, to say that there was not a single one among all who were included in the count who was unfit to go forth in the army — rather, all of them were mighty men of strength. And this is the meaning of His saying <b>all</b>: every single one of them goes forth to the army. And this is a miracle that does not occur among the nations, for it is impossible that among all their counts there should not be found even one who is unfit to go forth in the army."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:05:47.957534978Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}